# Hyperly — environment template
#
# No build-time environment variables are required. The Rust build no longer
# reads `.env`, and nothing from the environment is compiled into the binary
# (guarded by `scripts/secret-embedding-check.ts`).
#
# Provider keys, endpoints and prompts live in the app's own settings and local
# store — enter them in the UI. If a future workflow ever needs an environment
# value, read it at RUNTIME (`std::env::var` in Rust, `import.meta.env.VITE_*`
# for Vite) — never via `build.rs` / `env!()` / `option_env!()`.
